The corners of every widget whose own the reader did not choose:
one of `widgets::CORNER_CHOICES`;
automatic leaves each widget its own.

The ink of every widget whose own the reader did not choose: one of
`widgets::INKS`, a tone or a colour code;
automatic leaves each widget its own.

List the table of contents (op 7) in reading order, in bounded pages;
continue with the cursor of [`DocPage::end`]. `input` is 256 bytes;
`out` 4,096.

The format ids this reader shows, at most 8 (a page with more is refused);
none for every format (see
[`reads_every_format`](Self::reads_every_format)).

What happened to this book. For `can_delete`: `Ok` it can be deleted;
`Invalid` it is not a book; `NotFound` it is gone already (a delete only
forgets it); `Io` the card cannot. For `delete`: `Ok` it is deleted;
`Invalid` not a book; `State` it has annotations and `with_notes` was off;
`Busy` the host uses the path; otherwise the card's refusals.

When the row of button hints shows with the screen (see
[`ScreenDecl::hints`](crate::native::declare::ScreenDecl::hints));
not said: as the screen declared. Draft 38.
